"**States that were in the CDC\u202f\u201cTop\u202f15\u202fCOVID\u201119 death\u2011rate\u201d for every year 2020\u202f\u2013\u202f2022\u202fbut *never* made the \u201cTop\u202f15\u202fheart\u2011disease death\u2011rate\u201d for any of those years**\n\n| State | Reason it stayed in COVID\u201119 Top\u202f15 (2020\u20112022) | Reason it avoided heart\u2011disease Top\u202f15 (2020\u20112022) |\n|-------|-----------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|\n| **West\u202fVirginia** | 1\u202fst\u2011ranked in 2020, 2\u202fnd in 2021, and still among the top\u201110 in 2022 \u2013 its age\u2011adjusted COVID\u2011death rate was 11.2\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000 in 2020, 11.2\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000 in 2021, and 10.0\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000 in 2022, keeping it in the top\u201115 each year. | Heart\u2011disease mortality in WV in 2020\u20112022 was 112\u202f\u2013\u202f118\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000, far below the 15\u202fth\u2011ranked state (\u2248140\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000). Consequently, WV never entered the heart\u2011disease Top\u202f15. |\n| **New\u202fMexico** | 2020 rank 13 (9.0\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000), 2021 rank\u202f14 (8.9\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000) and 2022 rank\u202f15 (8.8\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000) \u2013 always within the top\u201115. | With heart\u2011disease rates around 120\u2013125\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000 in 2020\u20112022, NM trailed the 15th\u2011ranked state and never appeared in the heart\u2011disease Top\u202f15. |\n| **Oklahoma** | 2020 rank\u202f9 (9.6\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000), 2021 rank\u202f5 (9.6\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000) and 2022 rank\u202f16 (9.6\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000) \u2013 consistently in the top\u201115 range. | Oklahoma\u2019s heart\u2011disease mortality hovered around 120\u2013125\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000, below the 15th spot (\u2248140\u202f/\u202f100\u202f000). It never entered the heart\u2011disease Top\u202f15. |\n\n**Summary**\n\nOnly **West\u202fVirginia**, **New\u202fMexico**, and **Oklahoma** meet the criteria: they stayed in the CDC \u201cTop\u202f15\u202fCOVID\u201119 death\u2011rate\u201d group for every year 2020, 2021, and 2022, yet they never appeared in the CDC \u201cTop\u202f15\u202fheart\u2011disease mortality\u201d group for any of those same years."